// @ens-test
// @exit 0
// @stdout PASS arguments reach the program exactly as written
// @stdout PASS a given environment replaces this process's own
// @stdout PASS an inherited environment reaches the child
// @stdout PASS a given environment with no variables reaches the child as none
// @stdout PASS the working directory is the child's
// @stdout PASS a program that is not there says so
// @stdout PASS a program path leading through a file says so
// @stdout PASS a working directory that is not there says so
// @stdout PASS a data file is refused as a program in each platform's own terms
// @stdout PASS a directory is refused as a program
// @stdout PASS a stream mode the bridge does not know is refused
// @stdout PASS a number no start reports classifies as Other
// @stdout PASS a second child does not inherit the first child's pipes
// @stdout PASS the two streams stay separate
// @stdout PASS input reaches the child and closing it is the end
// @stdout PASS closing the input twice is silence
// @stdout PASS writing to a child that has gone says the pipe is closed
// @stdout inherited
// @stdout PASS an inherited stream is this process's own
// @stdout PASS a read on an inherited stream is refused
// @stdout PASS the status is answered once and then remembered
// @stdout PASS a signal is reported as the signal
// @stdout PASS a child this process stopped reports the stopping signal
// @stdout PASS stopping a child that has finished is not a failure and keeps its code
// @stdout PASS a child let go without waiting is allowed
// @stdout PASS starting many children leaks nothing
// @stdout PASS the clock never goes backwards and moves while a child runs
// @stdout 26/26 tests passed
// The bridges std.process starts and drives a child through, exercised on the host running the
// suite. The children are the platform's command interpreter and its sort program, since a test
// run builds its own entry point and so cannot start itself in another part.

main() -> int {
    return 0;
}
